{
  "description": "How every API Gateway route keeps its Lambda response under the 6 MiB cap. Policies: paginated (limit + next_token, pages cut to PAGE_BUDGET_BYTES), top_n (fixed caps, totals reported), summary (aggregates that do not grow with data), single_item (one stored item, size-checked where it can be large), bounded (small by construction). Routes rated at risk by the 2.41.0 audit name the volume test that proves the bound. Checked by lib/response-size.spec.ts (every API Gateway route) and lambda/api/test_route_size_policies.py (route maps, volume tests).",
